  "title": "IEEG004: A library of human electrocorticographic data and analyses (Kai J. Miller) - calibrated task subset",
  "description": "A BIDS-formatted subset of Kai J. Miller's library of human electrocorticographic (ECoG) data, covering six calibrated task archives: finger flexion, hand gestures, motor imagery, basic motor movement, and speech (verb generation and noun reading). It contains 111 recordings from 24 epilepsy patients with subdural electrode grids, recorded at 1 kHz at Harborview Hospital in Seattle. Signals are scaled to physical units and accompanied by events, channel, and electrode position files.",
  "methods_description": "Subdural ECoG was recorded from patients undergoing clinical monitoring for medically refractory epilepsy, using Synamps2 amplifiers at 1000 Hz with a built-in 0.15-200 Hz band pass and BCI2000 software. Source MATLAB files were converted to BrainVision format with MNE-BIDS. Data were scaled once to volts, and no filtering, resampling, or re-referencing was applied.",
